<title>UK: Zeneca submits Zomig for regulatory approval.</title>
<headline>Zeneca submits Zomig for regulatory approval.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bioscience specialist Zeneca Group Plc said on Wednesday that Zomig, its migraine treatment, had been submitted for regulatory approval in the U.S. and Europe.  </p>
<p>It said the clinical trial programme confirming efficacy and tolerability had been completed in over 4,000 patients treating over 50,000 migraine attacks.</p>
<p>The worldwide migraine treatment market is expected to reach 1.5 billion stg by the year 2000.</p>
<p>Zomig, formerly known as 311C90, was acquired from Glaxo Wellcome Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
